3.Insertion Sort 
works like sorting playing cards in your hand.

You take one element at a time and insert it into its correct position among the elements you've already sorted.
Main idea: Take an element, compare it with the elements on its left, shift bigger elements to the right, and insert the element in the correct position.


arr = [9, 46, 24, 52, 20, 13]

def insertion_sort(arr):
    n = len(arr)

    for i in range(1, n):
        key = arr[i]
        j = i - 1

        while j >= 0 and arr[j] > key:
            arr[j + 1] = arr[j]
            j -= 1

        arr[j + 1] = key

    return arr

print(insertion_sort(arr))


TC= O(n^2)
SC=O(1)
